# Auto-enter the Nix dev shell from flake.nix on `cd`.
# Requires direnv: https://direnv.net  (and `direnv hook <shell>` in your rc).
# Approve once with: direnv allow
#
# This replaced `source .venv/bin/activate`. There is no .venv in a fresh clone
# (nothing in the repo creates one, and flake.nix bakes every dependency into
# the interpreter instead), so that line made direnv fail on every `cd` into the
# repo -- which also meant the flake was never entered. `use flake` gives the
# same thing the venv was reaching for, plus the dev-* command map: run
# `dev-help` once you are in.
#
# use_flake is direnv stdlib (2.30+), so plain direnv is enough; nix-direnv only
# adds caching on top.
use flake
